  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 513.20 Gold Star Plate",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 513.20 Gold Star Plate.\n\n(a) Gold Star plates shall be issued to a vehicle owned or held in trust by a mother or stepmother of a person killed while on duty in the United States armed forces, pursuant to RSA 261:87-c.\n\n(b) A stepmother shall be eligible for a gold star plate under this rule if she:\n\n(1) Provides a marriage license which is dated prior to the armed service member’s 15th birthday; and\n\n(2) Provides a completed Department of Defense “DD form 1300” to the director.\n\n(c) If the vehicle is held in trust, the applicant shall provide a copy of the most updated trust document that demonstrates:\n\n(1) That the vehicle is owned by the trust, except that a current registration for the vehicle demonstrating that the vehicle held in the trust may be substituted for the trust document for this requirement; and\n\n(2) That the applicant is a trustee of the trust.\n\n(d) A gold star plate shall not be issued to a stepmother if a gold star plate is already issued to another stepmother for that service member.\n\nSource. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #12914, eff 11-16-19 (formerly Saf-C 514.19); ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 514.20)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
